{"title":"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_September_2025)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, September 2025)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1,_rewritten_and_completed\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1, rewritten and completed</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Motivation_for_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Motivation for Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(following_the_hint_from_the_discussion_page_[1])\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (following the hint from the discussion page [1])</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b66471dde29ff1899199de380d87c7927420db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2,\\cdots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive numbers, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a given real number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b921774aa821435f4a0826b849ebd6b402f11bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;q&lt;1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a258926ff9daba3d399f1be87dd4742595ceb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\cdots, b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> for which\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a98adce06afded515298a4ecf535894a591d3a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k&lt;b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83d5e09397d2b8ee5f1b9f38bffb35866884520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1,2,\\cdots, n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437d75b6b1cd3a6ed5e2a3fe4d3b8194f2b72ec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q&lt;\\dfrac{b_{k+1}}{b_k}&lt;\\dfrac{1}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"105\" height=\"41\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2ba10362c4a7bb37dc919b5d67569d7a942c5dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1,2,\\cdots,n-1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/7/d47f57482a9c791815feef3bd230f2836f778f81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1+b_2+\\cdots+b_n&lt;\\dfrac{1+q}{1-q}(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_n).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"361\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We notice that the constraints are linear, in the sense that if bi is a solution for ai, q, and bi' is a solution for ai', q, then for any k, k' &gt; 0 a solution for kai + k'ai', q is kbi + k'bi'. Also a \"near\" solution for ah = 1, other ai = 0 is b1 = qh-1, b2 = qh-2, ... , bh-1 = q, bh = 1, bh+1 = q, ... , bn = qn-h. \"Near\" because the inequalities in (a) and (b) are not strict.\n</p><p>However, we might reasonably hope that the inequalities would become strict in the linear combination, and indeed that is true. Define br = qr-1a1 + qr-2a2 + ... + qar-1 + ar + qar+1 + ... + qn-ran. Then we may easily verify that (a) - (c) hold.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_September_2025.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_September_2025)\">Remarks (added by pf02, September 2025)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, September 2025)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>1.  The solution above is unacceptable for several reasons:\n</p><p>It is unacceptable to write mathematical text without using\nparentheses, and writing indexes and powers in the line of\ntext, rather than use subscripts and superscripts.  On top\nof it, the \"solution\" is incomplete (the author uses \"we may\neasily verify\" to justify things which are not straightforward)).\nIt is also imprecise (the author uses the notion of `a \"near\"\nsolution...' without making it precise enough).\n</p><p>However, after a good amount of scrutiny and guessing, one\ncan see that the text contains a good idea.  Below I will\nrewrite the solution in a way a reader can make sense of it.\n</p><p>2.  The author of the above solution deleted a reference to\nthe discussion page <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p357934\">https://aops.com/community/p357934</a>.\nOn the discussion page there is an idea for another solution.\n(In all honesty, it is an idea, or a hint, but it can not be\ncalled a solution.)\n</p><p>3. Below I will discuss the above ideas, and give a more\ngeneral class of solutions to this problem.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.2C_rewritten_and_completed\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1,_rewritten_and_completed\">Solution 1, rewritten and completed</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1, rewritten and completed\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b568d3bbc6076c9a7444ac7a956b362433d6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = \\sum_{j = 1}^n q^{k - j} a_j = q^{k-1} a_1 + q^{k-2} a_2 + \\dots + a_k + \\dots + q^{n-k-1} a_{n-1} + q^{n-k} a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"583\" height=\"55\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79cde76e70f3f6e074da2b7e442743dfede9fd87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, \\dots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>To make things easy to follow, let us write this explicitly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec37f4048b4f92c2227c9bfe79fcb7d52ab99c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c406b9c932e83ff54ed50c8ec4aff3b5111608d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = a_1 + q a_2 + q^2 a_3 + q^3 a_4 + q^4 a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"273\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1ac299f422a6c8682181b9677e8271e0647b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2 = q a_1 + a_2 + q a_3 + q^2 a_4 + q^3 a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"265\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c54567ade8965bb24aa95b5056aa6a1732a2b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3 = q^2 a_1 + q a_2 + a_3 + q a_4 + q^2 a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"265\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34b1a520ba423712e38625093a1297a0312d4d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_4 = q^3 a_1 + q^2 a_2 + q a_3 + a_4 + q a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"265\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/9/c596a608cf33978b566b06124f6b3e115f481818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_5 = q^4 a_1 + q^3 a_2 + q^2 a_3 + q a_4 + a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"273\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let us verify that this is indeed a solution to the problem.\n</p><p>(a) is clearly true.  To verify (b), note that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we can suitably\ngroup terms in the expressions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc889bce614f45c6d9a71ad78c76026b2d609b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k, b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6106c21ffef460cf4bfbfb0313c1f0f4004880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = X + Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01fafad2bfb1d9c18354e3f3a514a699e02ab096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1} = q X + \\frac{1}{q}\\ Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc22bc84254cae8a1e965722b06bae7b0c5e15f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q &lt; \\frac{b_{k+1}}{b_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"72\" height=\"42\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4cd8c9e0fb3a943961da7c68f1c2a20d41faf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q &lt; \\frac{q X + \\frac{1}{q} Y}{X + Y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"112\" height=\"46\" />\nwhich becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/458262f98a426a48492b6cbaa152670f21dc2ac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q X + q Y &lt; q X + \\frac{1}{q}\\ Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"178\" height=\"42\" /> which is true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d7da959042a420689240e6eb6a48ba88bf0b91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />.\nSimilarly, it is easy to verify that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/97642d183b43391b803ddb51ddefd98287c3331a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b_{k+1}}{b_k} &lt; \\frac{1}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"76\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>To verify (c), note that when computing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615fe649abf68329093fc42d074e7746e08fde3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 + b_2 + \\dots + b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" /> and regrouping\nterms as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4ce4324a3165c29ac3c5f4e9499bf5c4386216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1 a_1 + S_2 a_2 + \\dots + S_n a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"17\" />, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e880b118bfa7c5db071a4ed8bb0890168702843f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and\none or two sums of successive powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.  More precisely,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/17934b789c7d660d6a4c157179c4e7974c8d23b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k = 1 + \\sum_{j = 1}^{n-1} q^j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"121\" height=\"58\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35a51f5f4479cf610e903ad871c5baa6f1fe9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = n$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9671ea36dfff151a9ef833b4acc5f817fb7bf26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k = 1 + \\sum_{j = 1}^{k-1} q^j + \\sum_{j = 1}^{n-k} q^j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"188\" height=\"58\" /> for other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb49db3f770f9339db2772fa0903b46b0952438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k &lt; 1 + q(1 + q^2 + ...) + q(1 + q^2 + ...) = 1 + 2 q \\frac{1}{1 - q} = \\frac{1 + q}{1 - q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"500\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Motivation_for_Solution_1\">Motivation for Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Motivation for Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the following related problem:\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e047bc14560bc613b17fb1ba735bba221764510a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9c151a661a687f6e3e9b6e95ff672c231b6ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />, not all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9952432253dd3c764faa67299b1e31546f1d710c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 0$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be\nsuch that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6eff5d0a97a53a14708616977e8ec249a65ec4f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; q &lt; 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a258926ff9daba3d399f1be87dd4742595ceb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\cdots, b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> such that\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a1224c5f7c05ef4d559f822bf88517050b676585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k \\le b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01bbd3a769ba5123cdb30ac36859c09eeb0e0e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1, 2, \\cdots, n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/4840accd0aed068491bb4acf84e8240a4d50f2e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q \\le \\frac{b_{k+1}}{b_k} \\le \\frac{1}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"109\" height=\"43\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d3402d88438987fdb6899662feca12fc457eb53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, 2, \\cdots, n-1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/40070cc68962ba730ad34ccda58a135c450e57f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 + b_2 + \\cdots + b_n \\le \\frac{1+q}{1-q}(a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_n).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"365\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>To solve this problem, first notice that we have some linearity:\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41b69b430f5d6935441f435f7be176730cc2d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\{b_1, b_2, \\dots, b_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" /> is a solution for given\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6528d15ad737efd1a9ee24670ddbd9fda3b7cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\{a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />, and similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a solution for\ngiven <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45b0deb0be09be0710f5dc4890e5475f3f64e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha B + \\beta B&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"19\" /> is a solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/5/d7596ecdb9a956fbe84e009e010a0e5bfb65278f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha A + \\beta A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"19\" />\nfor any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfac9941d66c5c95ba79b308ea19815ccbe5cb0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha, \\beta &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/539d04b38549aedc06772f67e4119103632f0c52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k = \\{0, 0, \\dots, 0, 1, 0, \\dots, 0\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"226\" height=\"20\" />, in other words,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d9674015097f7236214f3fa291aa57dbd61c754f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/9105c232fe350cb9c31373292da6c81af6adb8f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f407b4370b983f2a97897dafc421876a8229c8b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\ne k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />.  Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba53f1c42748a14499f9b946826f7db8b8b508b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_k = \\{q^{k-1}, q^{k-2}, \\dots, q, 1, q, \\dots, q^{n-k}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"301\" height=\"22\" /> is a solution to\nthis related problem for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7553256f94a2ce1069471dfe7c43bf8b7215ab90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a1c20b8ae44eaf812c3e674269f3e49e47b4243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\sum_{k=1}^n a_k A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"108\" height=\"53\" />, we should take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e7b977f4ef870e5592599dc29dc0998989eb89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\sum_{k=1}^n a_k B_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"109\" height=\"53\" />,\nwhich is a solution to both the related problem and the given, original\nproblem.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28following_the_hint_from_the_discussion_page_.5B1.5D.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(following_the_hint_from_the_discussion_page_[1])\">Solution 2 (following the hint from the discussion page <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p357934\">[1]</a>)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (following the hint from the discussion page [1])\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this solution we take\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/7/9376e8aac3be3055e083a519c0a72981d703c206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = a_k + \\sum_{j=1}^{\\frac{n-1}{2}} q^j (a_{[(k-j) \\mod n]} + a_{[(k+j) \\mod n]})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"361\" height=\"64\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> odd, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4215bc36f57fb51681003f39ca3c54d7574c42d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = a_k + \\sum_{j=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}-1} q^j (a_{[(k-j) \\mod n]} + a_{[(k+j) \\mod n]}) + q^{\\frac{n}{2}} a_{[k + \\frac{n}{2} \\mod n]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"501\" height=\"61\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> even.\n</p><p>To make things easy to follow, let us write this explicitly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec37f4048b4f92c2227c9bfe79fcb7d52ab99c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb7dace7ecc3a4280a1f6e233143c7bc9d185a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = a_1 + q a_2 + q^2 a_3 + q^2 a_4 + q a_5 = a_1 + q (a_5 + a_2) + q^2 (a_4 + a_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5bdde6dfc5d3e53b250e29e16dde028223ec08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2 = q a_1 + a_2 + q a_3 + q^2 a_4 + q^2 a_5 = a_2 + q (a_1 + a_3) + q^2 (a_5 + a_4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e5701acc2009e71a4e7f6b37f2641520f7ec965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3 = q^2 a_1 + q a_2 + a_3 + q a_4 + q^2 a_5 = a_3 + q (a_2 + a_4) + q^2 (a_1 + a_5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5947d9347b4649d3beaaa9f3097bca6fef8630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_4 = q^2 a_1 + q^2 a_2 + q a_3 + a_4 + q a_5 = a_4 + q (a_3 + a_5) + q^2 (a_2 + a_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cc445b1cc13b72cb0b2816316bd8ec568f4c4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_5 = q a_1 + q^2 a_2 + q^2 a_3 + q a_4 + a_5 = a_5 + q (a_4 + a_1) + q^2 (a_3 + a_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e326b48726d4c73525c3b980409600fd87ea9846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/6158c56a2ec0daaee438abfb61e96b728ce03b57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = a_1 + q a_2 + q^2 a_3 + q^3 a_4 + q^2 a_5 + q a_6 = a_1 + q (a_6 + a_2) + q^2 (a_5 + a_3) + q^3 a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"628\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/1/661843498bf6c544bdc67a65bd33d93870f22a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2 = q a_1 + a_2 + q a_3 + q^2 a_4 + q^3 a_5 + q^2 a_6 = a_2 + q (a_1 + a_3) + q^2 (a_6 + a_4) + q^3 a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"628\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d6cf17c6837494b6a90fc509895ebc9d2596ed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3 = q^2 a_1 + q a_2 + a_3 + q a_4 + q^2 a_5 + q^3 a_6 = a_3 + q (a_2 + a_4) + q^2 (a_1 + a_5) + q^3 a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"628\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f270d17af179199e974e2a61b0a3243ae3e454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_4 = q^3 a_1 + q^2 a_2 + q a_3 + a_4 + q a_5 + q^2 a_6 = a_4 + q (a_3 + a_5) + q^2 (a_2 + a_6) + q^3 a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"628\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60f18a3cdd2e2da9990c5d0f5fed012734f2474.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_5 = q^2 a_1 + q^3 a_2 + q^2 a_3 + q a_4 + a_5 + q a_6 = a_5 + q (a_4 + a_6) + q^2 (a_3 + a_1) + q^3 a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"628\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d096915a6638851002be51adaa8945593d294c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_6 = q a_1 + q^2 a_2 + q^3 a_3 + q^2 a_4 + q a_5 + a_6 = a_6 + q (a_5 + a_1) + q^2 (a_4 + a_2) + q^3 a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"628\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Proving that these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d6a4daa59851cdf057d7d865381f65e6e1c8377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\dots, b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy (a), (b), (c)\ngoes along the same lines as in Solution 1.  The only difference\nis that when comparing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9e9d4cc5fd858d837b4334ffb04e2f62819500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> in the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> odd, we\nnote that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we can suitably group terms in the expressions\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc889bce614f45c6d9a71ad78c76026b2d609b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k, b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/98751dc270a31f8bfc9653cf2694428385d0ac6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = X + Y + Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34324a53426d08f0db57e03384da9bb64f6be89b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1} = q X + Y + \\frac{1}{q}\\ Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"175\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc22bc84254cae8a1e965722b06bae7b0c5e15f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q &lt; \\frac{b_{k+1}}{b_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"72\" height=\"42\" /> becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5382814cac13af5ad81f4af532b8d7de22da3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q &lt; \\frac{q X + Y + \\frac{1}{q} Z}{X + Y + Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"147\" height=\"46\" /> which becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195f2a959d467e74f70cd9796462ee84110da7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q X + q Y + q Z &lt; q X + Y + \\frac{1}{q}\\ Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"258\" height=\"42\" /> which is true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d7da959042a420689240e6eb6a48ba88bf0b91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />.\nSimilarly, it is easy to verify that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/97642d183b43391b803ddb51ddefd98287c3331a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b_{k+1}}{b_k} &lt; \\frac{1}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"76\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution extracts the essence of the previous solutions,\nand thus generalizes them.\n</p><p>Think of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41b69b430f5d6935441f435f7be176730cc2d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\{b_1, b_2, \\dots, b_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6528d15ad737efd1a9ee24670ddbd9fda3b7cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\{a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />\nas column vectors, and consider the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6ec59fb66373824ad512c2dff849dffd515f99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = (q^{m_{ij}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />\nwith <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/08168a9d671e472178b03b00c19cd0131fa83858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{ij} \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>The following are sufficient conditions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, to imply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/274098275604c122f48fa9fd27c40241cb9d6bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = Q A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> is\na solution to the problem:\n</p><p>(1)  The diagonal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> has only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on it, and the non-diagonal elements\nof each column of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are positive powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8403d3ae27c483f641be006c91962b138055d25e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{ii} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6c61f0ae257a1ea290d0388f4c2e80a0d8ac6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{ij} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351d7a57c3c465e3e62c32332232067e2ebe1cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\ne j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>(2)  Every element of row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is either equal to the corresponding\nelement of row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, or differs from it by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> or of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8bbe4bee7c83c7ff4be58660ff2d03d6a9c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"40\" />.  In other words, for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/0887cc25ff30a2f73e2969a0aa9f1724581bb4dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{(k+1)j} = m_{kj}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />\nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4f055102f7468ae4360b003977b179309d57460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{(k+1)j} = m_{kj} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e2b54cd6af0a5ad235d14f493e1d34c6bdeec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{(k+1)j} = m_{kj} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>(3)  Each power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> appears at most twice.  In other words, here are no\ndistinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac6161840bffb116a04711a01cc080bb3b92fddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j_1, j_2, j_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25c57ce0d4902dbe38b2423af0267ea55ef3abc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{j_1k} = m_{j_2k} = m_{j_3k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"159\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Indeed, (1) implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac06a3bef7570e6d60157763c06719c10f403a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k &gt; a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />, so (a) is satisfied.  (2) implies that for\nany <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we can suitably group terms in the expressions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc889bce614f45c6d9a71ad78c76026b2d609b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k, b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> so\nthat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/98751dc270a31f8bfc9653cf2694428385d0ac6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = X + Y + Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34324a53426d08f0db57e03384da9bb64f6be89b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1} = q X + Y + \\frac{1}{q}\\ Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"175\" height=\"42\" />.  As we have\nseen, this implies (b).\n</p><p>(3) implies that when we group terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615fe649abf68329093fc42d074e7746e08fde3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 + b_2 + \\dots + b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" /> as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4ce4324a3165c29ac3c5f4e9499bf5c4386216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1 a_1 + S_2 a_2 + \\dots + S_n a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"17\" />, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e880b118bfa7c5db071a4ed8bb0890168702843f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and\none or two sums of distinct powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.  More precisely,\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de3011b2699ab9fd85134bce7937379f213e348b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k = 1 + q^{m_1} (1 + \\text{sum of distinct powers of q}) + q^{m_2} (1 + \\text{sum of distinct powers of q}) &lt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"658\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db13951d3b30705e0cd72b76ba66f6d58b2d720e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2q(1 + q^2 + ...) = 1 + 2 q \\frac{1}{1 - q} = \\frac{1 + q}{1 - q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"336\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>This proves (c).\n</p><p>There are very many matrices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> (different from the ones in solutions 1 and 2)\nsatisfying conditions (1), (2) and (3). Just as one example, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec37f4048b4f92c2227c9bfe79fcb7d52ab99c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> take\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245d8c6bd99545a7031066ebdc52327a3c2135f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\ \\ \\ q\\ \\ \\ q^2\\ \\ \\ q^3\\ \\ \\ q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d6bbdbf41ba81fc79634d68ecc62ff3c9f0326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q\\ \\ \\ 1\\ \\ \\ q\\ \\ \\ q^2\\ \\ \\ q^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5fd27f16eee9d3cd6631c80114f297cae98264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2\\ \\ \\ q\\ \\ \\ 1\\ \\ \\ q\\ \\ \\ q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645a19cc5572b54d19abbf3db904d73b0fa8619e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^3\\ \\ \\ q^2\\ \\ \\ q\\ \\ \\ 1\\ \\ \\ q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534fa2d78137035bd81e8cc41e0c8e58fb9854c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2\\ \\ \\ q^3\\ \\ \\ q^2\\ \\ \\ q\\ \\ \\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, September 2025]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO\" title=\"1973 IMO\">1973 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017111534\nCache expiry: 86400\nR